    "source_excerpt": "Miscarriage is common and can occur in any pregnancy for many different reasons. Taking acetaminophen at the recommended dose is not expected to increase the chance of miscarriage. One study found that using acetaminophen during pregnancy did not increase the chance of miscarriage, no matter when it was taken during pregnancy or for how long."
